<article class="env-lemma" id="0AY4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AY4">Lemma <span data-tag="0AY4">31.13.8</span>.</a> Let $X$ be an integral locally Noetherian scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$, $\mathcal{G}$ be coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. If $\mathcal{G}$ is reflexive, then $\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ X}(\mathcal{F}, \mathcal{G})$ is reflexive. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The statement makes sense because $\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ X}(\mathcal{F}, \mathcal{G})$ is coherent by Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01Y2" data-tag="01Y2">30.9.4</a>. To see the statement is true, see More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AV3" data-tag="0AV3">15.24.8</a>. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>